# VULNERABLE CONFIG (copy this to .htaccess to enable PHP execution on jpg/png)
# Attack Vector 2 — Apache AddType handler misconfiguration
#
# When this file is renamed to .htaccess inside the uploads/ directory,
# Apache will instruct mod_php to process ALL .jpg/.png/.gif files as PHP.
# Any uploaded JPEG that contains <?php ... ?> code will then be executed
# directly when requested via HTTP (no LFI needed).
#
# Real-world analogue: shared-hosting environments where .htaccess overrides
# are allowed inside user-writable upload directories.

AddType application/x-httpd-php .jpg .png .gif
